    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_leima_mesaya_shmuel",
     "kind": "mesaya",
     "gloss_en": "לימא מסייע ליה: one baraita excludes worms in dates and figs, the other includes worms in roots of olives and vines -- מאי לאו אידי ואידי בפירא, והא באביה והא שלא באביה? (67b.3)",
     "supports": "p_kishut_shehitlia_beibeha",
     "status": "rejected"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_al_haaretz_lehotzi_zizin",
     "gloss_en": "'upon the earth' -- to exclude the zizin in lentils, the gnats in kelisim, and the worm in dates and dried figs"
    }
   ]
  },
  "3": {
   "segId": "Chullin.67b.4",
   "sugya": "chullin_66b_snapir_vekaskeset",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support_deflection",
     "object": "defl_beilana_gufei",
     "gloss_en": "לא, אידי ואידי באביה: הא בפירא, הא באילנא גופא",
     "deflects": "s_leima_mesaya_shmuel",
     "refuted": false
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_okimta_ilana_gufei",
     "gloss_en": "no: both are while attached, and no difficulty: this one in the fruit, that one in the tree itself"
    }
   ]
  },
