    {
     "type": "objection_answer",
     "object": "ans_dagim_baasifa",
     "gloss_en": "הכי השתא? an animal is permitted by slaughter, which does not work for its worms; fish by gathering, and their worms grow in permittedness",
     "answers": "obj_mai_shna_darnim",
     "restores": "p_ravina_avla_li"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_dagim_baasifa",
     "gloss_en": "an animal becomes permitted by slaughter, and these [worms], since slaughter does not work for them, remain forbidden; but fish become permitted by mere gathering, and these, when they grow, grow in permittedness"
    }
   ]
  },
